Web search results for query: "Cloudflare Agents wrangler.jsonc Durable Objects configuration"

Links: [{"title":"Configuration · Cloudflare Agents docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/api-reference/configuration/"},{"title":"Getting started · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/get-started/"},{"title":"Environments · Cloudflare Durable Objects docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/reference/environments/"},{"title":"Configuration - Wrangler · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/configuration/"},{"title":"agents-starter/wrangler.jsonc at main · cloudflare/agents-starter","url":"https://github.com/cloudflare/agents-starter/blob/main/wrangler.jsonc"},{"title":"Prompting · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/get-started/prompting/"},{"title":"Continue • cloudflare/cloudflare-workers","url":"https://www.continue.dev/cloudflare/cloudflare-workers"},{"title":"Configuration · Cloudflare Pages docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/wrangler-configuration/"},{"title":"mcp-cloudflare/wrangler.jsonc at main · Pedropfuenmayor/mcp-cloudflare","url":"https://github.com/Pedropfuenmayor/mcp-cloudflare/blob/main/wrangler.jsonc"},{"title":"Bindings (env) · Cloudflare Workers docs","url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/bindings/"}]

Based on the search results, here's what I found about Cloudflare Agents, wrangler.jsonc, and Durable Objects configuration:

## Overview

The wrangler.jsonc file configures your Cloudflare Worker and its bindings.

## Durable Objects Configuration in wrangler.jsonc

For Cloudflare Agents, the wrangler.jsonc file needs to include Durable Objects bindings. Here's an example configuration that includes durable_objects with bindings specifying a name and class_name, along with migrations that define new_sqlite_classes for the Agent class.

A typical structure looks like:

```json
{
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      {
        "name": "Chat",
        "class_name": "Chat"
      }
    ]
  },
  "migrations": [
    {
      "tag": "v1",
      "new_sqlite_classes": ["Chat"]
    }
  ]
}
```

## Key Configuration Points

1. **Migrations**: Migrations tell Cloudflare how to set up storage for your Durable Objects, using the migrations array with a tag and new_sqlite_classes property.

2. **Agent Class Requirement**: You MUST set the value of migrations[].new_sqlite_classes to the name of the Agent class in wrangler.jsonc.

3. **Compatibility Flags**: Enabling Node.js compatibility mode is needed for agents, which agents depend on for crypto, streams, and other Node.js APIs.

The configuration enables your Agent to use Durable Objects for persistent storage and state management.


